{
  "requirement": "Before saving a record, the SDK replaces each dependency's `NodeId<D>` with the corresponding `D::NodeData`. When loading a record into an execution or checking it against a domain, the SDK interns each dependency's data in that domain's cache. Both conversions preserve the dependency kind, label, and observed fingerprint.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "One test, `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[saved_node_and_edge_inputs_survive_a_different_handle_allocation_order]`, covers every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.persisted_dependencies`. It is marked `{test}` for the requirement.\n\nSave direction (replace `NodeId<D>` with `D::NodeData`):\n- The test records a `Dependency::Node` on Node(2) and a `Dependency::OutgoingEdges` with label 7 on the subject. It saves them through `persist`.\n- It asserts that the stored record's `dependencies` equal `durable_inputs(&first, observed.dependencies())`. That helper maps each id to its cached data and clones the observed fingerprint and label.\n- This checks that ids are replaced by node data. It also checks that the kind (Node and OutgoingEdges), the label (7) and the observed fingerprint are preserved.\n\nLoad and check direction (intern in the domain's cache):\n- The test builds a `fresh` `Application` with a new `ValidationCache`. The `fresh` handles differ from the originals: it asserts `fresh.cache().node_data(subject)` is `None` and `fresh_target != target`.\n- It runs `saved.is_current(&fresh, ...)` and asserts it is true. This is the check against a domain.\n- It runs `validator.load_evidence(&descriptor)` and asserts the loaded dependencies match `[Node(fresh_target, _), OutgoingEdges(descriptor.source, 7, _)]`. This shows the data was interned in the fresh cache. The kinds and the label are preserved.\n- It asserts `durable_inputs(&fresh, loaded.dependencies()) == expected`. This covers the fingerprints, because `expected` carries the originals and `durable_inputs` clones the loaded ones.\n- `check_inputs(&loaded)` returns true. After the edges are cleared it returns false. So the loaded fingerprints are live and are really compared. A dropped or altered fingerprint would make the first check fail or the second pass.\n\nI found no untested obligation. Other tests in the file, such as `dependency_resolution_failures_do_not_execute_or_replace_saved_answers`, also assert the durable form with explicit fingerprints. No acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "3993505da5d50c39658c4c16c25c4fcfe79fef7a577e80a851fdedd1966f55f6",
